{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Cf1r5f7tdGa8XA1DPVo3m","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```json\n{\n  \"final_answer\": \"overclaim\",\n  \"evidence_tier\": \"clinical_human\",\n  \"conclusion_tier\": \"human_therapeutic\",\n  \"bridge_supported\": false,\n  \"assumptions\": [\n    \"Claim assumes SELECT enrolled adults without prior cardiovascular disease\",\n    \"Claim assumes the trial population matches 'overweight' descriptor\"\n  ],\n  \"steps\": [\n    \"Evidence states SELECT enrolled adults with 'established cardiovascular disease'\",\n    \"Claim states the trial was in adults 'who have never had cardiovascular disease'\",\n    \"These are directly contradictory population definitions\"\n  ],\n  \"alternative_hypotheses\": [\n    \"The claim may confuse SELECT with a different semaglutide trial (e.g., STEP trials which enrolled people without established CVD)\",\n    \"The claim may misremember the inclusion criteria of SELECT\"\n  ],\n  \"uncertainties\": [\n    \"Whether the claimant intended to reference a different trial\"\n  ],\n  \"key_claims\": [\n    \"SELECT establishes cardiovascular prevention with semaglutide\",\n    \"Population: adults with overweight who have never had cardiovascular disease\",\n    \"Evidence population: adults aged ≥45 with BMI ≥27 and ESTABLISHED cardiovascular disease\"\n  ],\n  \"self_check\": [\n    \"The evidence explicitly states 'established cardiovascular disease' as an inclusion criterion\",\n    \"The claim explicitly states 'never had cardiovascular disease'\",\n    \"This is a fundamental factual error about the trial population, not a matter of interpretation\",\n    \"The cardiovascular benefit shown (HR 0.80) is in a secondary prevention population, not primary prevention as claimed\"\n  ],\n  \"confidence\": 0.98\n}\n```\n\n**Explanation:** The claim contains a critical factual error. SELECT enrolled adults with *established* cardiovascular disease (secondary prevention), not adults who \"have never had cardiovascular disease\" (primary prevention). This is a direct contradiction of the trial's inclusion criteria. While SELECT did demonstrate cardiovascular benefit with semaglutide, the claim mischaracterizes the population in which this benefit was demonstrated, making it an overclaim that exceeds and misrepresents the evidence."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":843,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":518,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}}